review:
Play the game;
It crashes;
save file is corrupted;
GG always be maindenless

Tedious gameplay before getting to actual fights;
Paths to bosses can be filled with enemies, and getting to some optional bosses requires knowing exactly where that boss is and annoying clearing before.

they don't tell you anything;
I just ran around at first, didn't archive anything. There are golden lines pointing somewhere. Hidden chest? Side quest? They didn't say anything. Then I wasn't able to find one mandatory boss, convinced he's not nearby, friend had to guide me to him.

unbalanced game;
my friends immediately told me not to use summons since with them all bosses are apparently brute-forceable. So to get a boss experience I have to as a new player know summons are broken.

bosses are meh, one is above average;
against some bosses I was just able to spam kill them with a suboptimal built (dex without shield and without arcane)
some have a tedious path to them which is more frustrating than hard
the imo best boss has a second phase which is a lot more difficult and needs time to recognize dodge patterns. problem is I always needed to get through the first phase so at some point I had all moves and dodge patterns memorized which again, was more tedious than hard

the world building is cool;
nice fantasy world with dragons and skeletons and such

ultimately I haven't bothered with the last boss since all the previous ones were tedious. Not recommended.
